{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "cues": [
    {
      "id": "oklo-v4-r2-cue-1",
      "transcript": "About two billion years ago, Earth had nuclear reactors. Nobody built them.",
      "file": "audio/oklo-v4-r2/narration/cue-1.wav",
      "start": 0,
      "duration": 5.35,
      "beatIndex": 0,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "oklo.asset.natural-reactors.script.1",
      "samples": 128400,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "oklo-v4-r2-cue-2",
      "transcript": "In 1972, uranium from Gabon held less uranium-235 than expected.",
      "file": "audio/oklo-v4-r2/narration/cue-2.wav",
      "start": 5.666666666666667,
      "duration": 7.425,
      "beatIndex": 1,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "oklo.asset.natural-reactors.script.2",
      "samples": 178200,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "oklo-v4-r2-cue-3",
      "transcript": "Fission fingerprints in the rock revealed ancient nuclear reactions. How could geology sustain them?",
      "file": "audio/oklo-v4-r2/narration/cue-3.wav",
      "start": 13.266666666666667,
      "duration": 6.95,
      "beatIndex": 2,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "oklo.asset.natural-reactors.script.3",
      "samples": 166800,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "oklo-v4-r2-cue-4",
      "transcript": "Back then, uranium had a higher share of that easily split isotope. Geology concentrated it into rich deposits.",
      "file": "audio/oklo-v4-r2/narration/cue-4.wav",
      "start": 20.533333333333335,
      "duration": 8.325,
      "beatIndex": 3,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "oklo.asset.natural-reactors.script.4",
      "samples": 199800,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "oklo-v4-r2-cue-5",
      "transcript": "Splitting uranium released neutrons. Collisions with hydrogen in groundwater slowed them, helping them split more uranium.",
      "file": "audio/oklo-v4-r2/narration/cue-5.wav",
      "start": 29.033333333333335,
      "duration": 8.475,
      "beatIndex": 4,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "oklo.asset.natural-reactors.script.5",
      "samples": 203400,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "oklo-v4-r2-cue-6",
      "transcript": "Enough avoided escape or absorption elsewhere to keep the chain going.",
      "file": "audio/oklo-v4-r2/narration/cue-6.wav",
      "start": 37.7,
      "duration": 4.825,
      "beatIndex": 5,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "oklo.asset.natural-reactors.script.6",
      "samples": 115800,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "oklo-v4-r2-cue-7",
      "transcript": "From one studied zone's isotopes, researchers infer starts and stops: heating drove water away; cooling let it return.",
      "file": "audio/oklo-v4-r2/narration/cue-7.wav",
      "start": 42.7,
      "duration": 8.4,
      "beatIndex": 6,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "oklo.asset.natural-reactors.script.7",
      "samples": 201600,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "oklo-v4-r2-cue-8",
      "transcript": "Reaction zones in rock. Heat, not electricity. Earth had assembled the conditions for fission, without machinery.",
      "file": "audio/oklo-v4-r2/narration/cue-8.wav",
      "start": 51.4,
      "duration": 8.1,
      "beatIndex": 7,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "oklo.asset.natural-reactors.script.8",
      "samples": 194400,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    }
  ],
